      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64908ffac974920a1fecd872",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think any sort of desync should be eliminated in principle because that is a very roundabout and convoluted way to simulate a player visibility toggle. A better solution would be to have player visibility exposed directly in Udon, and toggled via a boolean, rather than exploiting a failed ownership check in a black box component (VRC Station) to desync their transform in order to obscure their visibility with some sort of clipping or culling or simply obscured behind a wall or floor.\n\nPlus, it violates the general principle of object ownership and object transform syncing. You cannot move or apply forces on remote players because you do not have the object ownership, and there is no reason why you should be able to override their transform, via any method, to create a desync situation the whole ownership system is designed to eliminate.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
